// About
"about_heading" = "About";
"about_body" = "Senior iOS Engineer with 6+ years of professional experience, plus 2 earlier years shipping production code while studying for my engineering degree, completed in July 2021. I take full ownership of features and architecture, from the first call to the release: I modernize legacy codebases, build for accessibility, and treat testing as part of the craft, not an afterthought. At Alaska Airlines I made an assistive hardware keypad drive VoiceOver on airport bag tag stations. On the App Store since 2018 with four shipped apps across iPhone, iPad and Mac. Recently I have carried that ownership past the app layer, into AI agentic workflows and hardware-software integration. I own two products end to end: Sideshore, a wind forecast app on iPhone, iPad and Mac from one native SwiftUI target, and Zhen, an open-source macOS network scanner written entirely in Swift 6.";
"about_personal" = "Away from the keyboard I edit video in Final Cut Pro, which I used to do for short films as a student, make music in GarageBand, and go climbing.";
"about_availability" = "Available now, freelance or full-time.";
"about_citizenship" = "Dual Mexican–Spanish citizen.";

// Experience
"exp_heading" = "Experience";

"exp1_role" = "Independent iOS Development & Consulting";
"exp1_company" = "Self-directed";
"exp1_meta" = "Dec 2024 – Present";
"exp1_desc" = "Designed, built and shipped Sideshore to the App Store: a wind forecast and live-station app on iPhone, iPad and Mac from one native SwiftUI target, with an in-house Swift package that handles all networking on device (request merging, rate limiting, retries, disk cache for offline). Built and open-sourced Zhen, a native macOS network scanner written entirely in Swift 6: an engine, command line and privileged helper in one Swift package, a notarized SwiftUI app on top, and a pre-registered measurement study behind its timing model. Shipped MythLog to the Mac App Store. Delivered a client project end-to-end: a book app for a writer, built in Flutter. Shipped AI and agentic workflows into production apps and tooling (Claude, OpenAI, xAI, Ollama), and trained on Apple's Foundation Models framework. Also build and operate After Dark Stories, a production web product on server-side Swift.";

"exp2_role" = "Senior Software Engineer";
"exp2_company" = "Alaska Airlines";
"exp2_meta" = "Dec 2023 – Nov 2024";
"exp2_desc" = "Worked on the iPad software behind Alaska's self-service bag tag stations, about 330 stations in 79 airports across the US. Owned accessibility for the station and drove a11y adoption on the team: integrated the Storm Interface assistive keypad with VoiceOver, mapping its keys as keyboard input to drive navigation and speech. Built the station's local-network layer, with the iPad managing TCP connections to the Aila scanner enclosure and the bag tag printer, and implemented MRZ passport reading on the Aila hardware end to end. Built the app to work within the stations' MDM-managed iPad setup. Maintained older applications built on custom in-house passport-scanning frameworks.";

"exp3_role" = "Senior iOS Engineer";
"exp3_company" = "Peek.com";
"exp3_meta" = "Aug 2021 – Aug 2023";
"exp3_desc" = "Built the bookings grid: a fully dynamic rows-and-columns view, server-driven and rendered in real time, that handles up to 10,000 bookings with shadows and animations intact, now in use across the US. Migrated parts of a decade-old marketplace app to SwiftUI as part of its gradual migration, on MVVM, Clean Architecture and Coordinators. Wrote automated UI tests (Robot Pattern + XCUITest) and worked on the GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline. Integrated GraphQL and connected WiFi terminal hardware to the app. Led features from start to finish as project lead. Mentored engineers on the team.";

"exp4_role" = "Co-founder & Software Engineer";
"exp4_company" = "Xplain";
"exp4_meta" = "Aug 2020 – Aug 2021";
"exp4_desc" = "Co-founded the company with friends and led its engineering: a 100% Swift product (Vapor backend, iOS front end, shared Swift libraries between the two) shipping two production iOS apps in SwiftUI and UIKit with secure Stripe payment flows.";

"exp5_role" = "Full Stack Engineer (iOS Focus)";
"exp5_company" = "Sunwise";
"exp5_meta" = "Jun 2019 – Aug 2020";
"exp5_desc" = "Delivered production iOS features end-to-end in Swift and Objective-C against REST APIs, with full production responsibility, held alongside my final university coursework.";

"exp6_role" = "Full Stack Engineer";
"exp6_company" = "DaCodes";
"exp6_meta" = "Aug 2018 – Jun 2019";
"exp6_desc" = "First engineering role: built full-stack applications for agency clients on AWS, concurrent with university coursework.";

